# Source manifest — reproducible-by-reference (Invariant 3).
# Re-clone at build time; the working tree under sources/ruff/ is gitignored.
#
# TOOLCHAIN SOURCE — a tool this repo actually RUNS (#81, ingested 2026-08-02).
#
# ⚠️ INVARIANT: this pin MUST track the version we actually run.
#   version source: pyproject.toml `[dependency-groups] dev` EXACT pin `ruff==0.16.4`,
#                   confirmed against `uv run ruff --version`. It was a floor
#                   (`ruff>=0.11`) when this manifest was written; the group moved to
#                   exact pins, so the old wording named a constraint that no longer
#                   exists and would send the next bumper to the wrong line.
#   pinned here:    0.16.5
# A pin that drifts from the installed version makes the corpus answer questions
# about code we are not running. Not hypothetical — `sources/graphify.manifest`
# records exactly that failure: it sat two releases behind for weeks, so every
# "how does graphify work?" answer came from the wrong source.
#
# Pin the RELEASE TAG, never a branch head — a branch drifts ahead of the release.
# To bump: change the version in its source above, then
#   git ls-remote --tags --refs https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff | grep <version>
# and set ref/commit here to match, then `mise run kb-build`.
#
# kind = code: AST extraction only, no LLM, no cost. NOTE this extracts the
# SOURCE and skips every .md by design — the tool's DOCS are a separate
# `kind = docs` mirror (#123), not this manifest.
url = https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff
ref = 0.16.5
commit = 9e4938c4a60bed3e87a11ee1e1db1bd23f4d964a
kind = code
added = 2026-08-02
build = defer
defer_reason = #654: measured by `mise run kb-extract-census` on graphify 0.9.53, 2026-09-02 — re-measured after the fork rebase and UNCHANGED from 0.9.50. 289 syntax-error files. ruff is a LINTER, so its fixture corpus is deliberately malformed by design — the biome case (#654) at a quarter the size. Registering 289 individually justified entries is the wrong shape for a fixture tree. NOTE the clearing condition is NOT #654's: ruff has ZERO collisions, so sibling-extension disambiguation would change nothing here. This clears only when a fixture tree can be accepted as a CLASS rather than per file -- not by a manifest edit and not by a version bump; the v0.9.50 -> v0.9.53 rebase changed none of these figures. (An earlier version of this field named both conditions at once, which the cold review of 69c126cbaef8 flagged: a deferral whose stated remedy cannot apply to it never clears.)
